From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winebus, ntoskrnl, ntdll: PS5: an Xbox controller is also Windows' HID gamepad, so every API finds it.

With an Xbox controller chosen (the default), a game got the controller only through XInput (patch 0470): the PS5 bus made
no HID device, so DirectInput, raw input, SDL (its RAWINPUT and HIDAPI drivers), Rewired and Windows.Gaming.Input's HID
path found no controller at all, only the keyboard and mouse (players' reports: ONE PIECE Grand Gourmet, Nine Sols, MOUSE:
P.I. For Hire, Super Lone Survivor; the owner's Ys Origin, a 32-bit DirectInput 8 game, 2026-11-02). On Windows an Xbox
controller is both: XInput, and the HID gamepad its driver makes, "HID\VID_045E&PID_028E&IG_00", which DirectInput lists
as "Controller (XBOX 360 For Windows)" with X/Y, Rx/Ry, the triggers on one Z axis, ten buttons and a hat, and which SDL
and other programs that also use XInput recognise by "IG_" and do not count twice.

- winebus bus_ps5: while an Xbox kind is the title's (pw_wine_pad_kind; until it sets one, WINE_PS5_CONTROLLER), the bus
  makes that gamepad, 045e:028e or 045e:02ea, from the title's pad slot (pw_wine_pad), in Windows' layout
  (PS5_Proton wine/ps5/pw_wine_xusb.h, the layout of Wine's winexinput.sys with a 32-bit logical maximum): a report each
  time the slot's packet moves, released and centred while no controller is connected. Switching kinds removes it and
  makes the other (the control overlay, patch 2472); the DualSense, when chosen, as before.
- winebus main.c: such a device's id ends in "&IG_00", told from its ids while the PS5 bus runs (WINE_PS5_HID), not from a
  new device_desc field: that struct crosses to winebus's Unix half, and on a console whose two halves came from
  different builds the shifted layout faulted a stock mouse's start in winedevice (a8rel81-base-2026-11-02-e1).
- ntoskrnl pnp.c: the bus's Xbox gamepad is installed as its DualSense is (no inf), and its interface gets the same
  per-program link (patch 2401); wine_ps5_hid_start waits up to a second for it, as for the DualSense, so a game that
  looks for controllers once, at its start, finds it.
- ntdll loader.c: WINE_PS5_HID=live starts the bus in every game's process, a helper's too (patch 2472 started it only in
  the title's), since the Xbox gamepad is needed wherever a game runs. Wine's own programs still start none.
- ntdll file.c: a program opens its own link to the Xbox gamepad, as to the DualSense (patch 2401).
XInput is unchanged: it reads the title's slot and never this device, so a game that uses both sees one controller.
Windows.Gaming.Input still finds no Xbox controller (Wine's takes Xbox pads only from winexinput's "&XI_" device).
Base PS5 13.60, input-base-2026-11-02-01 (tests/pad-api-probe.c): Xbox 360 and Xbox One, 32 and 64 bits, in a helper and in the
title, and a new prefix's first session: XInput, DirectInput 8 ("Controller (XBOX 360 For Windows)" 045e:028e, or the Xbox
One's 02ea), raw input (IG_) and winmm all have the controller, every reading centred at rest; a Cross reaches DirectInput
and winmm 6-21 ms after XInput. The device is there 60-142 ms after the bus starts. Ys Origin, a DirectInput 8 game, takes the
controller and moves through its title menu with either Xbox kind.
